{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JBTeEvEf3w2TZ55NET7f3z","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"TLE9201SG pinout PG-DSO-12 pin 2 VSO DIR PWM DIS datasheet\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Infineon Technologies Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A SPI搭載Hブリッジ\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.jp/infineon-tle9201sg/\"},{\"title\":\"Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Bridge with SPI\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.pe/infineon-tle9201sg/\"},{\"title\":\"Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Bridge with SPI\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.pl/infineon-tle9201sg\"},{\"title\":\"Infineon Technologies Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Brücke mit SPI\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.de/infineon-tle9201sg\"},{\"title\":\"Infineon Technologies Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Brücke mit SPI\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.ch/infineon-tle9201sg\"},{\"title\":\"Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Bridge with SPI\",\"url\":\"https://nl.mouser.com/en/infineon-tle9201sg/\"},{\"title\":\"Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Bridge with SPI\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.in/en/infineon-tle9201sg/\"},{\"title\":\"Infineon is the driver for DC motor control PWM to 20 kHz and maximum current of 7 A\",\"url\":\"https://www.radiolocman.com/news/new.html?di=150800\"},{\"title\":\"Infineon Technologies Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Brücke mit SPI\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.li/infineon-tle9201sg\"},{\"title\":\"12-BSOP; P/PG-DSO-12\",\"url\":\"https://punchouttest.digikey.kr/en/products/detail/infineon-technologies/TLE9201SGAUMA1/6560041\"}]\n\nThe search didn't return the TLE9201SG pin-by-pin table, so I can't confirm what pin 2 is, the VSO, DIR, PWM, or DIS assignments, or the pin numbering. The results only cover general product information.\n\n- **Package and control:** Distributor listings describe the device as a 6A H-bridge in the PG-DSO-12-17 package, with a heat slug for thermal performance. PWM/DIR control reduces the number of PWM capable pins needed on the microcontroller side. That suggests the DIR and PWM inputs are the two control pins, but the results don't show which physical pins they occupy.\n- **PWM:** The outputs can be pulse width modulated at frequencies up to 20kHz.\n- **Diagnostics:** It's protected against short circuits and overtemperature and provides extensive diagnosis via SPI or basic error feedback via error flag.\n- **Package listing:** A DigiKey listing gives the package as 12-BSOP with exposed pad, supplier device package PG-DSO-12-17, and an operating supply range of 5V to 28V. It also doesn't include a pinout.\n- **Conflicting current rating:** One news summary gives the current-limit threshold as 7A typical and calls the part a 5A bridge in its opening line, while Mouser lists 8A typical and 6A output. The datasheet should settle this.\n\nTo get the pin 2, VSO, DIR, PWM, and DIS assignments, check the pin configuration section of the Infineon TLE9201SG datasheet directly, or search for \"TLE9201SG pin configuration\" to find it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d040c4d-5f77-495d-8ec4-cf62a703d8c8","uuid":"61ba935f-7680-48f2-9e27-e180e0c5f3be","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:43:35.867Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"TLE9201SG pinout PG-DSO-12 pin 2 VSO DIR PWM DIS datasheet","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01RuCEMMg5u3T5TkEzenNBGK","content":[{"title":"Infineon Technologies Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A SPI搭載Hブリッジ","url":"https://www.mouser.jp/infineon-tle9201sg/"},{"title":"Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Bridge with SPI","url":"https://www.mouser.pe/infineon-tle9201sg/"},{"title":"Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Bridge with SPI","url":"https://www.mouser.pl/infineon-tle9201sg"},{"title":"Infineon Technologies Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Brücke mit SPI","url":"https://www.mouser.de/infineon-tle9201sg"},{"title":"Infineon Technologies Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Brücke mit SPI","url":"https://www.mouser.ch/infineon-tle9201sg"},{"title":"Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Bridge with SPI","url":"https://nl.mouser.com/en/infineon-tle9201sg/"},{"title":"Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Bridge with SPI","url":"https://www.mouser.in/en/infineon-tle9201sg/"},{"title":"Infineon is the driver for DC motor control PWM to 20 kHz and maximum current of 7 A","url":"https://www.radiolocman.com/news/new.html?di=150800"},{"title":"Infineon Technologies Infineon Technologies TLE9201SG 6A H-Brücke mit SPI","url":"https://www.mouser.li/infineon-tle9201sg"},{"title":"12-BSOP; P/PG-DSO-12","url":"https://punchouttest.digikey.kr/en/products/detail/infineon-technologies/TLE9201SGAUMA1/6560041"}]},"The search didn't return the TLE9201SG pin-by-pin table, so I can't confirm what pin 2 is, the VSO, DIR, PWM, or DIS assignments, or the pin numbering. The results only cover general product information.\n\n- **Package and control:** Distributor listings describe the device as a 6A H-bridge in the PG-DSO-12-17 package, with a heat slug for thermal performance. PWM/DIR control reduces the number of PWM capable pins needed on the microcontroller side. That suggests the DIR and PWM inputs are the two control pins, but the results don't show which physical pins they occupy.\n- **PWM:** The outputs can be pulse width modulated at frequencies up to 20kHz.\n- **Diagnostics:** It's protected against short circuits and overtemperature and provides extensive diagnosis via SPI or basic error feedback via error flag.\n- **Package listing:** A DigiKey listing gives the package as 12-BSOP with exposed pad, supplier device package PG-DSO-12-17, and an operating supply range of 5V to 28V. It also doesn't include a pinout.\n- **Conflicting current rating:** One news summary gives the current-limit threshold as 7A typical and calls the part a 5A bridge in its opening line, while Mouser lists 8A typical and 6A output. The datasheet should settle this.\n\nTo get the pin 2, VSO, DIR, PWM, and DIS assignments, check the pin configuration section of the Infineon TLE9201SG datasheet directly, or search for \"TLE9201SG pin configuration\" to find it."],"durationSeconds":6.33841258600002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JBTeEvEf3w2TZ55NET7f3z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AVJhUxm9idmVtSJhwHTwn6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MAX9924 pinout uMAX-10 IN+ IN- BIAS COUT OUT datasheet variable reluctance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Web Analytics\",\"url\":\"https://aiema.cn/part/datasheet/max9924uaubv-fn21434623\"},{\"title\":\"Analog Devices MAX9924UAUB+T\",\"url\":\"https://fat.lcsc.com/product-detail/C5145181.html\"},{\"title\":\"Electronic Components Datasheet Search |\",\"url\":\"https://html.alldatasheet.com/html-pdf/415678/MAXIM/MAX9924_11/3333/21/MAX9924_11.html\"},{\"title\":\"forum.arduino.cc\",\"url\":\"https://forum.arduino.cc/t/max9924/655708\"},{\"title\":\"Maxim Integrated Operationsverstärker Oberfläche 1.4 MHz μMAX, biplor typ. 5.5 V, biplor typ. 4.5 V, 10-Pin Nein\",\"url\":\"https://at.rs-online.com/web/p/operationsverstarker/1904819\"},{\"title\":\"Maxim Integrated Operationsverstärker Oberfläche 1.4 MHz μMAX, biplor typ. 5.5 V, biplor typ. 4.5 V, 10-Pin\",\"url\":\"https://ch.rs-online.com/web/p/operationsverstarker/1904819\"},{\"title\":\"jlcpcb.com\",\"url\":\"https://jlcpcb.com/partdetail/154964-MAX9924UAUB/C143633\"},{\"title\":\"azcus.digikey.com\",\"url\":\"https://azcus.digikey.com/en/products/detail/analog-devices-inc-maxim-integrated/MAX9924UAUB-V-T/3517058\"},{\"title\":\"Maxim Integrated Operationsverstärker Oberfläche 1.4 MHz μMAX, biplor typ. 5.5V, biplor typ. 4.5 V, 10-Pin\",\"url\":\"https://de.rs-online.com/web/p/operationsverstarker/1905379\"},{\"title\":\"Web Analytics\",\"url\":\"https://v1.aiema.cn/part/datasheet/max9924uaubt-fn8234037\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up the official MAX9924 datasheet pin table, so I can't confirm the pinout from the manufacturer's document. The results do include a forum post that lists a full pin assignment:\n\n- **Pin assignments (per a user's forum post):** Pin 1 is IN+, Pin 2 is IN-, Pin 4 is BIAS, Pin 7 is COUT, Pin 10 is VCC, and Pins 5 and 6 are GND and ZERO_EN. Pins 3 and 8 are no-connect, and the post also lists EXT and INT_THRS (Pin 7 (COUT) 10K --> 5V pullup). This is a user's wiring, not the datasheet itself, so verify it against the source.\n- **BIAS:** A forum member quoting the datasheet says that a well-decoupled external resistor-divider generates a VCC/2 signal for the BIAS input. The same quote says BIAS should be bypassed with capacitors, so tying it straight to ground, as that poster did, looks wrong. The post's author reported COUT stuck at 5 V, which the forum thread was trying to diagnose.\n- **Package and device type:** The part is listed as a 10-pin uMAX package, and the family is described as Variable Reluctance Sensor Interfaces with Differential Input and Adaptive Peak Threshold. Distributors list the uMAX-10 package with a Sensor Interface IC Differential Input Logic Output type.\n- **Datasheet availability:** Mirror sites such as alldatasheet and AiEMA host copies of the MAX9924 datasheet, which is about 23 pages. The package information shows the uMAX 10-pin package code as U10+2 (outline 21-0061) (10 µMAX U10+2 21-0061 90-0330).\n\nI didn't find any source that uses the name \"OUT\" for this pin, so the output pin appears to be COUT. For an authoritative pin diagram, check the Analog Devices/Maxim MAX9924 datasheet directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d040c4d-5f77-495d-8ec4-cf62a703d8c8","uuid":"1184c6ff-d0e8-493e-8593-9dcf895eba56","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:43:37.647Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"MAX9924 pinout uMAX-10 IN+ IN- BIAS COUT OUT datasheet variable reluctance","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Q7eTKch1JJ9jrKUuY4cEWk","content":[{"title":"Web Analytics","url":"https://aiema.cn/part/datasheet/max9924uaubv-fn21434623"},{"title":"Analog Devices MAX9924UAUB+T","url":"https://fat.lcsc.com/product-detail/C5145181.html"},{"title":"Electronic Components Datasheet Search |","url":"https://html.alldatasheet.com/html-pdf/415678/MAXIM/MAX9924_11/3333/21/MAX9924_11.html"},{"title":"forum.arduino.cc","url":"https://forum.arduino.cc/t/max9924/655708"},{"title":"Maxim Integrated Operationsverstärker Oberfläche 1.4 MHz μMAX, biplor typ. 5.5 V, biplor typ. 4.5 V, 10-Pin Nein","url":"https://at.rs-online.com/web/p/operationsverstarker/1904819"},{"title":"Maxim Integrated Operationsverstärker Oberfläche 1.4 MHz μMAX, biplor typ. 5.5 V, biplor typ. 4.5 V, 10-Pin","url":"https://ch.rs-online.com/web/p/operationsverstarker/1904819"},{"title":"jlcpcb.com","url":"https://jlcpcb.com/partdetail/154964-MAX9924UAUB/C143633"},{"title":"azcus.digikey.com","url":"https://azcus.digikey.com/en/products/detail/analog-devices-inc-maxim-integrated/MAX9924UAUB-V-T/3517058"},{"title":"Maxim Integrated Operationsverstärker Oberfläche 1.4 MHz μMAX, biplor typ. 5.5V, biplor typ. 4.5 V, 10-Pin","url":"https://de.rs-online.com/web/p/operationsverstarker/1905379"},{"title":"Web Analytics","url":"https://v1.aiema.cn/part/datasheet/max9924uaubt-fn8234037"}]},"The search didn't turn up the official MAX9924 datasheet pin table, so I can't confirm the pinout from the manufacturer's document. The results do include a forum post that lists a full pin assignment:\n\n- **Pin assignments (per a user's forum post):** Pin 1 is IN+, Pin 2 is IN-, Pin 4 is BIAS, Pin 7 is COUT, Pin 10 is VCC, and Pins 5 and 6 are GND and ZERO_EN. Pins 3 and 8 are no-connect, and the post also lists EXT and INT_THRS (Pin 7 (COUT) 10K --> 5V pullup). This is a user's wiring, not the datasheet itself, so verify it against the source.\n- **BIAS:** A forum member quoting the datasheet says that a well-decoupled external resistor-divider generates a VCC/2 signal for the BIAS input. The same quote says BIAS should be bypassed with capacitors, so tying it straight to ground, as that poster did, looks wrong. The post's author reported COUT stuck at 5 V, which the forum thread was trying to diagnose.\n- **Package and device type:** The part is listed as a 10-pin uMAX package, and the family is described as Variable Reluctance Sensor Interfaces with Differential Input and Adaptive Peak Threshold. Distributors list the uMAX-10 package with a Sensor Interface IC Differential Input Logic Output type.\n- **Datasheet availability:** Mirror sites such as alldatasheet and AiEMA host copies of the MAX9924 datasheet, which is about 23 pages. The package information shows the uMAX 10-pin package code as U10+2 (outline 21-0061) (10 µMAX U10+2 21-0061 90-0330).\n\nI didn't find any source that uses the name \"OUT\" for this pin, so the output pin appears to be COUT. For an authoritative pin diagram, check the Analog Devices/Maxim MAX9924 datasheet directly."],"durationSeconds":7.143129150000022,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AVJhUxm9idmVtSJhwHTwn6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
