{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PPzjs4rtd4g6PbkFzucXem","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MAX9924 \"INT_THRS\" \"EXT\" pin \"connect\" internal threshold datasheet\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MAX9924–MAX9927-Variable Reluctance Sensor Interfaces ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.com/datasheet/2/609/1/MAX9924_MAX9927-3471190.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MAX9924–MAX9927-Variable Reluctance Sensor ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX9924-MAX9927.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"General Description The MAX9924–MAX9927 variable reluctance (VR or mag-\",\"url\":\"https://www.mouser.com/datasheet/2/256/MAX9924-MAX9927-79049.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MAX9924U Eval Kit Datasheet by Maxim Integrated\",\"url\":\"https://www.digikey.jp/htmldatasheets/production/524763/0/0/1/max9924u-eval-kit.html\"},{\"title\":\"MAX9924–MAX9927-Variable Reluctance Sensor ...\",\"url\":\"https://static.chipdip.ru/lib/601/DOC028601581.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"General Description The MAX9924U evaluation kit (EV kit) is a fully assem-\",\"url\":\"https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX9924UEVKIT.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MAX9924 Datasheet(PDF) - Maxim Integrated Products\",\"url\":\"https://www.alldatasheet.com/datasheet-pdf/pdf/255006/MAXIM/MAX9924.html\"},{\"title\":\"General Description The MAX9924–MAX9927 variable reluctance (VR or mag-\",\"url\":\"http://www.es.co.th/Schemetic/PDF/MAX9924-MAX9927.PDF\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) MAX9926 Datasheet - (MAX9924 - MAX9927) Variable Reluctance Sensor Interfaces\",\"url\":\"http://www.datasheet.es/PDF/643603/MAX9926-pdf.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the MAX9924–MAX9927 variable reluctance sensor datasheet, and its mode table answers the INT_THRS and EXT wiring question.\n\n- **Mode selection:** The device's mode is set by the voltages on ZERO_EN and INT_THRS. The MAX9924/MAX9926 provide four modes of operation: Mode A1, Mode A2, Mode B, and Mode C.\n- **Pin wiring per mode:** In the mode table, Mode A1 has both ZERO_EN and INT_THRS at VCC, Mode A2 has both at GND, Mode B has ZERO_EN at VCC and INT_THRS at GND, and Mode C has ZERO_EN at GND and INT_THRS at VCC (Table rows as listed in the datasheet's mode table).\n- **EXT in each mode:** The datasheet says to leave EXT unconnected in Modes A1, A2. Apply an external voltage in Modes B, C.\n- **Mode B behavior:** An external threshold voltage is applied at EXT allowing application-specific adaptive algorithms to be implemented in firmware.\n- **INT_THRS pin role:** The pin description lists it as Internal Adaptive Threshold. Mode configuration pin.\n- **Reference design:** One result shows the MAX9924 wired in Mode A2 with EXT unconnected, and another shows the EV kit's jumper table with EXT on the 1-2 position for Modes A1/A2 and 1-3 for Mode B (the EV kit's MODE A1, A2, B, and C configuration table).\n\nCaveat: the snippets are fragmentary and some pin-function text is split across pages, so check the table and pin description in the full datasheet (Analog Devices or Mouser copy) before relying on exact pin assignments. The MAX9925/MAX9927 variants have per-channel INT_THRS1/INT_THRS2 and EXT1/EXT2 pins, so use the correct part number.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d040c4d-5f77-495d-8ec4-cf62a703d8c8","uuid":"7243ae5e-8dc7-41af-aa88-a1e97400f032","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:50:10.612Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"MAX9924 \"INT_THRS\" \"EXT\" pin \"connect\" internal threshold datasheet","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01WoYxuf98qPMKptea4uMNju","content":[{"title":"MAX9924–MAX9927-Variable Reluctance Sensor Interfaces ...","url":"https://www.mouser.com/datasheet/2/609/1/MAX9924_MAX9927-3471190.pdf"},{"title":"MAX9924–MAX9927-Variable Reluctance Sensor ...","url":"https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX9924-MAX9927.pdf"},{"title":"General Description The MAX9924–MAX9927 variable reluctance (VR or mag-","url":"https://www.mouser.com/datasheet/2/256/MAX9924-MAX9927-79049.pdf"},{"title":"MAX9924U Eval Kit Datasheet by Maxim Integrated","url":"https://www.digikey.jp/htmldatasheets/production/524763/0/0/1/max9924u-eval-kit.html"},{"title":"MAX9924–MAX9927-Variable Reluctance Sensor ...","url":"https://static.chipdip.ru/lib/601/DOC028601581.pdf"},{"title":"General Description The MAX9924U evaluation kit (EV kit) is a fully assem-","url":"https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX9924UEVKIT.pdf"},{"title":"MAX9924 Datasheet(PDF) - Maxim Integrated Products","url":"https://www.alldatasheet.com/datasheet-pdf/pdf/255006/MAXIM/MAX9924.html"},{"title":"General Description The MAX9924–MAX9927 variable reluctance (VR or mag-","url":"http://www.es.co.th/Schemetic/PDF/MAX9924-MAX9927.PDF"},{"title":"(PDF) MAX9926 Datasheet - (MAX9924 - MAX9927) Variable Reluctance Sensor Interfaces","url":"http://www.datasheet.es/PDF/643603/MAX9926-pdf.html"}]},"The search turned up the MAX9924–MAX9927 variable reluctance sensor datasheet, and its mode table answers the INT_THRS and EXT wiring question.\n\n- **Mode selection:** The device's mode is set by the voltages on ZERO_EN and INT_THRS. The MAX9924/MAX9926 provide four modes of operation: Mode A1, Mode A2, Mode B, and Mode C.\n- **Pin wiring per mode:** In the mode table, Mode A1 has both ZERO_EN and INT_THRS at VCC, Mode A2 has both at GND, Mode B has ZERO_EN at VCC and INT_THRS at GND, and Mode C has ZERO_EN at GND and INT_THRS at VCC (Table rows as listed in the datasheet's mode table).\n- **EXT in each mode:** The datasheet says to leave EXT unconnected in Modes A1, A2. Apply an external voltage in Modes B, C.\n- **Mode B behavior:** An external threshold voltage is applied at EXT allowing application-specific adaptive algorithms to be implemented in firmware.\n- **INT_THRS pin role:** The pin description 